# Commitments — Memory

*Last updated: {{YYYY-MM-DD}} (manual)*

> **Worklist only** (Memory v2). The exocortex's most-touched file, kept small on purpose (≤24 KB, enforced by `tools/memory_maint.py`).
> - One row per item, forever. IDs (`C-NNNN`) are permanent — get the next one with `python3 tools/memory_maint.py next-id C`.
> - `Slug` is the `EXO_DONE::<slug>` acknowledgment key.
> - `Note` is ≤160 chars and holds **current state only**. No history in rows, no run notes, no "STATUS <date>" lines, no day counts — `memory/INDEX.md` computes ages, and history goes to `memory/journal/`.
> - Closing = set `State`, set `Touched` to today, move the row to `Closed (last 7 days)`. The script archives it to `memory/archive/commitments/YYYY-MM.md` a week later.
> - Rows open 21+ days are flipped to `CHRONIC` by the script: one compact line in briefings, one Keep / Accept / Reframe question in the weekly review, no daily nagging.

